# Cloudflare Pages response headers (paths are matched per rule; every matching
# rule's headers apply, and a header set twice is joined with a comma — for
# Content-Security-Policy that means both policies are enforced, so keep the
# demo's own meta policy and this one compatible).
#
# Baseline CSP for the whole site. The allowlists are the origins the built
# site actually loads (audited 2026-10-13 against `hugo --minify` output and
# the live edge, which also injects Cloudflare Web Analytics):
#   - script: gtag (googletagmanager.com) and the edge-injected
#     static.cloudflareinsights.com beacon. There is NO 'unsafe-inline' in
#     script-src (aifocus-5wrp): the inline scripts the build produces are
#     pinned by sha256 hash instead, so an injected inline <script> does not
#     run. The list is generated, never hand-edited - `node tools/csp-hashes.mjs`
#     rewrites it from the built HTML and `--check` (gate signal 6) fails when it
#     drifts. Two consequences worth knowing before editing this line:
#       * adding an inline <script> to a template or a static page needs the
#         regeneration step, or the browser will block it;
#       * inline EVENT HANDLER attributes (onload=, onsubmit=, oninput=) are
#         governed by the same directive, so the two that used to be here
#         (the font preload and the newsletter form) are now bound in
#         assets/js/site.js, and the calculator demos bind theirs in their own
#         hashed scripts.
#     The demo pages narrow this on their own meta policy, whose script-src is
#     'self' only, and the intersection is what applies there.
#     The X embed (/setting-goals/, and the home/list pages that render its
#     full content) loads platform.x.com/widgets.js, which pulls its chunks
#     from platform.twitter.com and JSONP data from cdn.syndication.twimg.com.
#   - style/font: the Joan webfont pair, plus 'unsafe-inline' for the theme's
#     inline styles.
#   - img: 'self' plus data: URIs; https: is left open so a post can still
#     reference an external image without a header change.
#   - media: local files plus data: URIs — /web-uplift-report/ inlines a small
#     data:video/mp4 clip.
#   - frame: the embeds posts actually use (YouTube, paulkinlan.github.io,
#     esper.val.run, wasm-vs-js.paulkinlan-ea.deno.net, and X's
#     platform.twitter.com / platform.x.com / syndication.twitter.com post
#     iframes) and same-origin, for the in-page demos.
#   - connect: analytics endpoints, Cloudflare's beacon, and the three provider
#     APIs. The provider hosts are here because the demo's own meta policy
#     allows exactly one of them and policies intersect: without them in this
#     policy the demo's sends would be blocked outright.
#   - frame-ancestors is 'self', not 'none': /agent-do-my-agent-loop/ embeds
#     /where-prompts-run-demo/ in a same-origin iframe. Cross-origin framing is
#     still denied, which is what the clickjacking exposure was about.
#   - style keeps 'unsafe-inline' on purpose: 71 style="" attributes across the
#     built site cannot be pinned without 'unsafe-hashes', so style injection
#     remains possible where an injection sink exists - script execution, the
#     part that reaches credentials and sessions, does not. THREAT_MODEL.md
#     section 4 states that limit rather than implying it away.
#
# REVERTING the script-src hashes (one line, no other change needed): delete the
# 'sha256-...' tokens from script-src above and put 'unsafe-inline' back next to
# 'self'. Nothing in the build reads the hashes; tools/csp-hashes.mjs only owns
# the tokens it generated. Doing so re-opens aifocus-5wrp, so amend
# THREAT_MODEL.md section 4 in the same change.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-1yaycBk9N0R+ggenS5Snwwm3Nosg5SnLNtPh0Y/ONDk=' 'sha256-IUF3flK8YOXAXiwsBdzPtrEb5Mi8yBxnpPuTa1YW8Dg=' 'sha256-OT2C8mkjTtfzbjeIOx4yQUhK/H3bQfY3DiLBBQSS08Q=' 'sha256-T7B18n5lxUhbQdNBJOMpVgtViMai6phFZbBSqJnPzVE=' 'sha256-UxmpDf96BRANnG2uioRrZUyBYQBxVTw6JXsijOKYuQM=' 'sha256-XYSBS7QVYxodoRCm0dstngA8RIonU+PO8OK28obd5HY=' 'sha256-XZJ5QZwNESjYTa1H/RWGFj1MqpcgnV/BESybTdHC/Wc=' 'sha256-Z5nurmmHOIy72MaDvzSXnibRi/6uJKXvjiykPwBPH4s=' 'sha256-ap3HAFeug9jJwukUXPy9TO0Uk2GN1afAvak6bdysY7A=' 'sha256-c61fgmN10IlDZ5hnrG+k5W7Qg/08TyvmHul2WwzG4NU=' 'sha256-qipDdYsSgI7TH/vUwXOfAGKUn26ye8OpeqpDGHDtOws=' 'sha256-rkq5eLFWY/E5ajRUXsw8MUUpcug0gbIfyP21695sVLA=' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://platform.x.com https://platform.twitter.com https://cdn.syndication.twimg.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https:; media-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://region1.google-analytics.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://api.anthropic.com https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com https://api.openai.com; frame-src 'self' https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://www.youtube.com https://paulkinlan.github.io https://esper.val.run https://wasm-vs-js.paulkinlan-ea.deno.net https://platform.x.com https://platform.twitter.com https://syndication.twitter.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://buttondown.com; frame-ancestors 'self'

# Moderation page: keep it out of search indexes and caches. Access control is
# a Cloudflare Access application on /admin/* and /api/admin/*.
/admin/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Cache-Control: no-store

# Share-card pages exist only to be screenshotted into og:image
# (functions/og/[[path]].js); keep them out of search results.
/*/og-card.html
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
